# whitelist file for block-badips
#
# Each IPv4 or IPv6 address or range which is in a separate line will never be
# blocked by block-badips.sh, even if it is on the downloaded list, in
# /etc/block-badips.blacklist, or part of a blocked range.
# Lines containing anything else, like these comments, are ignored.
#
# Examples:
#192.0.2.10
#198.51.100.0/24
#2001:db8::10
#2001:db8:1::/48
127.0.0.1
